{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1002033-developing-the-admonitoria-concept","id":1002033,"title":"Developing the Admonitoria Concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-11T18:37:10-08:00","id":1002033,"title":"Developing the Admonitoria Concept","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I really like the Admonitoria concept and hope it will be explored/developed further. To promote it, I introduced two vampire type fairies in the Fae Entitites thread. Also, here are some ideas for merits to give Admonitoria characters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Taste of Blood (2 dots)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Academics 3, investigate 1, and either science or occult 3.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> By tasting a targets blood, they can get a great deal of genetic information from them. This includes ethnicity, heritage, lifespan, strengths and weaknesses, and whether they suffer from a genetic flaw.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Redcaps (3 dots)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Note: I am aware that the description of Admonitoria states that they cannot store vitae/glamour, but perhaps that can be edited. It would allow the player to explore the concept of how some types of fae (Redcaps being the most well known) use blood to charge their spells/magic. I think it would be cool if it was revealed that the Admonitoria had their own unique form of blood magic.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Academics 3, Occult 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The Admonitoria can store blood in a device, usually a cap, to use in their Thaumaturgy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Scent of Blood (3 or 5 dots)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Blood Potency 1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>Like sharks, the Admonitoria have a keen sense of smell for blood. at the three dot version, the Admonitoria is always aware whenever at least a drop of blood is spilled. At the five dot version, the Admonitoria can sense when life is nearby. No roll is necessary for either level of this merit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Doppelg\u00e4nger</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Taste of Blood, Blood Potency 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> The Admonitoria can take the form of any individual whose blood they have drunk. <i>Note: If they drink the blood of a supernatural being like a mage or werewolf, they can\u2019t mimic their supernatural abilities. Though they CAN mimic the blessings of changelings.</i></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:48:31-08:00","id":1002078,"title":"","content":"What's the benefit of redcap over just drinking blood and storing the glamour/blood within themselves like they already can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:58:03-08:00","id":1002084,"title":"","content":"I envision the Redcap merit being used by the Admonitoria to power their Thaumaturgy spells. Truthfully, I think it would be really cool if the Admontoria practiced their own unique form of blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:05:57-08:00","id":1002095,"title":"","content":"But why would they do that for their blood sorcery when they can just use their own blood pool for it. Its spending three xp for no actual benefit.<br /> <br /> As for Admonitora having their own magic, the blood sorcery book makes it rather easy to make new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-12-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:11:18-08:00","id":1002097,"title":"","content":"Good Point. Maybe Recap can be used to enhance their Thaumaturgy in another way. Do you have any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:17:19-08:00","id":1002101,"title":"","content":"Another thought, the write states that an Admonitoria's mien is not much different from a pure fae character. However, I believe their should be something that allows them to be distinguished. Maybe they are as pale as a corpse and are beginning to give off some decay. Maybe a Admonitoria who is tied to the Gangrel clan is unable to take a pure human form and their default form is some beast man mode?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:17:58-08:00","id":1002244,"title":"","content":"Fae are such diverse creatures that it's hard to really give these guys anything that would conclusively say &quot;this is no ordinary Changeling&quot;.<br /> <br /> But maybe a Buffy-esque &quot;Game Face&quot; whenever they feed or use Disciplines?<br /> <br /> And a conspicuous lack of any traits both physical and psychological that could be tied to one of the other Seemings.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the psychological differences would stand out the most. From what I can tell, they have little to nothing human left in them. Both vampires and changelings have intregity-equivalents that deal with their level of humanity, but Admonitoria have Balance, which is about balancing their two entwined -monstrous- natures. That wouldn't make them evil, but they would definitely think in a way totally detached from mundane humanity, torn between the mind of the predator and the call of the Wyrd. It would be something that someone who knew about Changelings and spent any significant amount of time with one would probably notice sooner or later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T19:45:07-08:00","id":1002749,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Claws of the Beast (2 dots)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Blood Potency 3<b>, </b>Gangrel Heritage</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> Calling on the powers of the beast, the Admonitoria unsheathes three inch long claws that deal aggravated damage. Unlike pure vampires, who can only use <i>claws of the unholy </i>while frenzying, the Admonitoria can use these claws by spending a point of glamor/vitae.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Drawback:</b> this power puts the vampire and fairy nature out of line, so the Admonitoria must make a five dice balance roll when using this ability.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Attuned to the Elements (1 to 3 dots)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Protean 2, Blood Potency 3, Gangrel heritage</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>The Admonitoria can adjust to extreme environments; such as extreme heat or cold, the ability to breath underwater, or the ability to adjust to and survive in caverns hundreds of miles below the Earth surface. Each dot in this merit allow him to adjust to one type of extreme environment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Beasts of Legend (1 to 2 dots)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Protean 4, Blood Potency 5, Gangrel heritage.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>This power allows the Admonitoria to become of the fae monsters of legend. These include not just generic monsters like dragons, griffons, and unicorns, but also manticores, chimera\u2019s, hell hounds, man beast forms similar to those of werewolves and other shape shifters, or even some Lovecraftion abomination. The Admonitoria can become one legendary beast per dot The Admonitoria gains all the powers of dice bonuses associated with the beast.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Drawback:</b> Along with the powers and strengths of the monster whose form you take, you also gain their frailties and weaknesses.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:26:15-08:00","id":1004600,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I had some more ideas for Admonitoria merits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Through the Looking Glass(3)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Obscufate 4, Blood potency 4, Mekhet/Nosferatu heritage</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>By Spending a point of glamour/vitae, the Admonitoria can banish a target to the Hedge. With an exceptional success, they can banish a target to Arcadia.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Boogeyman</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Nightmare 4, Blood Potency 4, Nosferatu heritage.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> you take the form of your targets greatest fear.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T09:23:35-08:00","id":1004977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1002033-developing-the-admonitoria-concept?p=1004600#post1004600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#000000]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect: </b>By Spending a point of glamour/vitae, the Admonitoria can banish a target to the Hedge. With an exceptional success, they can banish a target to [B]Arcadia[?B].</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that's basically perma-death, right? For 1 Glamour and a lucky dice roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:52:28-08:00","id":1005502,"title":"","content":"One thing I have thought about is what happens to an Amonitoria when they lose all balance. I don't see them turning into <i>True Fae, </i>rather I see them turning into something similar to a Lunar Exalted's Chimera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:41:44-08:00","id":1005565,"title":"","content":"All that's coming to mind from that description is a powerful blood-sucking hobgoblin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:44:53-08:00","id":1005568,"title":"","content":"Do you have any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"h